  N17_Idempotency [label="IDEMPOTENCY CHECKS BEFORE OUTPUT
================================
Before writing outputs:
- check whether an equivalent plan already exists under OUTPUT_ROOT or source pack
- if it exists and ALLOW_OVERWRITE=no, create a versioned plan or ask for confirmation
- same manifest plus same live snapshot should produce same plan
- if plan changes, record exactly which manifest or live-state fact changed
- do not duplicate plan IDs silently
- do not silently promote blocked items
- do not silently convert Codex-required work into deterministic applier work
- do not overwrite prior plan artifacts.", color="#F9A825", fillcolor="#FFFDE7"];
  N18_Safety [label="SAFE COMMANDS / FORBIDDEN ACTIONS
=================================
Allowed in CIP05:
- read uploaded/sandbox files
- read manifest and config-state snapshot
- read provided SPEC/ANX/hook material
- produce sandbox plan artifacts
- produce proposal-only Codex pack requirements
- list deterministic tooling candidates without implementing them

Forbidden in CIP05:
- edit config files
- edit public tooling
- edit main DOT or CIP DOT files
- mutate private evidence or companion outputs
- run bootstrap, mount, pull, push
- run Docker, Runpod, paid APIs, package installs, env creation, broad smoke, or live infra
- read or print credential contents
- apply any plan
- assert successful implementation.", color="#BF360C", fillcolor="#FBE9E7"];
  N19_ResponseFormat [label="REQUIRED RESPONSE FORMAT
========================
Current phase: CIP05 config implementation planning
Selected DOT:
Addressed role:
Variable block proposed/confirmed:
Manifest read:
Config-state snapshot read:
Required source contract status:
Manifest/snapshot consistency:
Items planned:
Items no-op/already covered:
Items blocked or human-design required:
Patch classes selected:
Application modes selected:
Allowed/forbidden surface summary:
CIP06 eligibility summary:
Outputs created/proposed:
Safety status:
Decision: PASS / STOP
Recommended next route:", color="#37474F", fillcolor="#ECEFF1"];
  N20_PassStop [label="PASS / STOP CONDITIONS
======================
PASS only if:
- variables confirmed
- CIP03 manifest read
- CIP04 snapshot read
- ANX05/ANX06/implementation-plan hook source contract applied or fallback noted
- manifest/snapshot consistency checked
- each actionable item has one primary patch class
- application mode selected per item
- allowed and forbidden surfaces listed
- preflight/validation/post-smoke plan defined where actionable
- CIP06 eligibility decided
- output artifact contract satisfied or proposed
- no forbidden mutation occurred.

STOP if:
- user has not confirmed
- manifest is missing or contradictory
- config-state snapshot is missing/stale for approved items
- manifest approves a surface not represented in snapshot and no safe plan can be made
- requested action is immediate config mutation, public tooling edit, DOT edit, evidence mutation, bootstrap, mount, pull, push, package install, env creation, live infra, credential read, or destructive action
- output would overwrite existing artifact with ALLOW_OVERWRITE=no.

After PASS:
Do not silently run CIP06. Recommend CIP06 only for items eligible under the plan and only with explicit operator confirmation.", color="#B71C1C", fillcolor="#FFEBEE"];
  N21_Reentry [label="RE-ENTRY INTO CIP AND V7 PIPELINE
=================================
If all items are no-op/already-covered, route may stop after verification evidence or proceed to CIP06 verify-only closeout if desired.

If items require Codex-pack implementation, produce or route to an implementation-pack creation step before CIP06 application.

If items are eligible for deterministic tooling later, record candidates for future 0C/tooling extraction, but do not implement tooling in CIP05.

If items are blocked/human-design, route back to CIP01/CIP02 for richer request evidence or to an operator design step.

If the plan is approved for application, the next route is CIP06 idempotent application and closeout. CIP06 remains mutation-default=no and must ask for explicit confirmation again.", color="#333333", fillcolor="#F5F5F5"];
